## 🔧 Development Best Practices

### 1. Documentation-Driven Development

**Before Writing Code:**
- Read project documentation (AGENTS.md, DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md)
- Understand the feature/requirement fully
- Plan the implementation approach

**While Writing Code:**
- Document variables inline
- Add comments explaining complex logic
- Use descriptive task names

**After Writing Code:**
- Update role README.md
- Update CHANGELOG.md
- Add usage examples

### 2. Iterative AI Collaboration

**Initial Generation:**
```
Developer: "Generate an Ansible task for X"
AI: [generates basic task]
Developer: Reviews and identifies improvements needed
```

**Refinement:**
```
Developer: "Add error handling and make it idempotent"
AI: [adds block/rescue and changed_when]
Developer: Reviews and tests
```

**Final Polish:**
```
Developer: "Add comprehensive documentation"
AI: [adds inline comments and variable docs]
Developer: Final review and commit
```

### 3. Testing Mindset

**Always Test:**
- Syntax: `ansible-playbook --syntax-check`
- Linting: `ansible-lint`
- Dry run: `ansible-playbook --check`
- Real run: `ansible-playbook` (on test environment)
- Idempotency: Run twice, verify no changes second time

**Test Matrix:**
| Distribution | Relay Type | Status |
|--------------|------------|--------|
| Ubuntu 22.04 | Standard | ✅ |
| Ubuntu 22.04 | Exit | ✅ |
| Ubuntu 22.04 | SOCKS | ✅ |
| Debian 11 | Standard | ✅ |
| Fedora 38 | Standard | ✅ |

