## 🛡️ Code Quality Standards

### Idempotency Checklist
- [ ] Tasks specify explicit `state` parameter
- [ ] Shell commands use `changed_when`
- [ ] File operations use proper modules (file, copy, template)
- [ ] Services use service/systemd modules
- [ ] Tested by running playbook twice

### Security Checklist
- [ ] No secrets in plaintext
- [ ] Ansible Vault used for sensitive data
- [ ] File permissions appropriate (600/644/755)
- [ ] `no_log: true` for sensitive operations
- [ ] Input validation for user-provided values

### Documentation Checklist
- [ ] Task names are descriptive
- [ ] Variables documented in defaults/main.yml
- [ ] Role README.md complete
- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated
- [ ] Inline comments for complex logic

